hat:<br>100 < 77j + 38 < 500</p><p>Subtract 38 from all parts of the inequality:<br>100 - 38 < 77j < 500 - 38<br>62 < 77j < 462</p><p>Now divide all parts by 77:<br>62 / 77 < j < 462 / 77<br>0.805... < j < 6</p><p>The integers j that satisfy this inequality are j = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5.</p><p>We are looking for the smallest possible integer sum N in the specified range. This corresponds to the smallest possible integer value of j in the range of possible j values, which is j = 1.</p><p>Substitute j = 1 into the general form for N:<br>N = 77(1) + 38 = 77 + 38 = 115.</p><p>Let's verify that N = 115 is within the range and satisfies the remainder conditions:<br>100 < 115 < 500 (Condition 1 satisfied)<br>115 ÷ 7 = 16 with remainder 3 (115 = 16 * 7 + 3) (Condition 2 satisfied)<br>115 ÷ 11 = 10 with remainder 5 (115 = 10 * 11 + 5) (Condition 3 satisfied)</p><p>Since 115 is the value of N for the smallest valid integer j (j=1), it is the smallest integer sum satisfying all conditions.</p><p>The dollar amount allocated for immediate funding is this smallest possible integer sum.</p>",
